// Title: Potential EventLog File Location Tampering
// Sigma ID: 0cb8d736-995d-4ce7-a31e-1e8d452a1459
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: D3F7A5105
// Date: 2023-01-02 | Modified: 2023-08-17
// ATT&CK: defense-impairment, T1685.001
// Description: Detects tampering with EventLog service "file" key. In order to change the default location of
//   an Evtx file. This technique is used to tamper with log collection and alerting
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/eventlog/eventlog-key
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/registry/registry_set/registry_set_evtx_file_key_tamper.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where (RegistryKey endswith "\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\EventLog*" and RegistryKey endswith "\\File") and (not(RegistryValueData contains "\\System32\\Winevt\\Logs\\"))
